Of the six dimensions decomposed, only domain exposure significantly affects cross-attack detection at full conversation length. Classification supervision, label correctness, label granularity, and temporal modeling are non-factors; domain specificity is marginal (1\,pp gap at full length, though 8\,pp at $K$=2). Practitioners need continued pretraining on domain text, not annotation pipelines or specialized temporal architectures.

